1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
*Piano music*

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,620
Good morning church. Good morning. I gotta apologize before we get started. Donovan's leaving I think though, so that's okay.

3
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:46,380
I've had some sniffles, so if I sniff one to the microphone, I'm maybe not as good as Dr. Kumar.

4
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:51,560
So bear with me. Don't leave, but bear with me.

5
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:59,860
This morning, oh, for those of you that don't know me, my name is Corey Smith and I have the privilege of

6
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:04,440
serving on the teaching team here at Canvas Community Church. So if this is your first time, welcome.

7
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:10,880
Glad you're here with us. We've kind of been going through, as you can see in the slide there, our summer series in the Book of Psalms.

8
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:18,880
We're gonna take a little detour today, maybe better said, we're gonna be diving into a mini-series within the series

9
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:29,720
on a special collection of books known as the Psalms of Ascent. These 15 Psalms, which we'll start in today and ending at, well, we're starting 120

10
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:37,860
and we'll end at 134 today. Provide a historical worship set for the people of God as they traveled together to Jerusalem.

11
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:44,800
We'll see these, and there's a lot of tongue twisters today, so again, bear with me. Psalms, songs, it's the whole thing.

12
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:48,180
So you might get a, you might guess, you guys might get a laugh out of it today.

13
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:54,140
But these Psalms, they provide a historical worship set for people as they traveled together to Jerusalem.

14
00:01:55,080 --> 00:02:01,340
As we'll see, these Psalms were songs of travelers, not just solo adventurers, but whole communities making the journey together

15
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:06,640
from wherever they were to worship the maker of heaven and earth in Jerusalem.

16
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:12,480
And as we talk about journeys this morning, I can't help but think that some of our regular attenders may be watching

17
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:17,040
from the mountains or the beach or wherever your summer travels have taken you.

18
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:23,760
I think some journeys, like vacations or bucket lists, trips,

19
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:29,440
you plan for months.

20
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:35,480
You've got the itinerary, you've mapped the route, you've made the packing list and the playlist,

21
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:39,040
and you can't wait to just get started.

22
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:45,700
But other journeys that I think people in the room have probably experienced, maybe even bigger journeys,

23
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:50,500
begin because something inside you says, I just can't stay here anymore.

24
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:56,800
You may not know exactly where you're going yet, but you know you just can't stay put.

25
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:00,860
And I don't know where you find yourself today, and I don't know what kind of journey you've been on lately,

26
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:04,640
but my hope, and I know it sounds cliche, so I acknowledge that,

27
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,160
is that you'll view this life as a journey.

28
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:10,220
And more specifically, as a follower of Jesus,

29
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:14,220
that you'll view this life as a journey with God and his community.

30
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:18,780
Some trips have destinations that are worth every step.

31
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:22,220
Others, the journey itself has been better than the arrival.

32
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:25,660
And sometimes, if we're honest,

33
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:29,580
either the road or the destination has lived up to the expectation.

34
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,520
But here's the thing I've learned.

35
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:35,940
When I look back on trips, the things I remember most aren't the pictures at the end.

36
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:36,960
They're a nice reminder.

37
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,240
But typically, for me,

38
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,540
they're the moments along the way.

39
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:43,380
The conversations in the car,

40
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,900
the wrong turns that became unexpected detours,

41
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,900
the laughter, the jokes,

42
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,860
even the arguments

43
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:53,040
that, strangely enough,

44
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,700
drew us closer.

45
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:58,040
Now, Samantha hates when I say this,

46
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,300
but it's less about the destination

47
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:01,140
and more about the journey.

48
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:03,340
To be honest,

49
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,600
she hates it because I usually say it sarcastically

50
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,860
when I veer off course to go to the place I want to go.

51
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:10,200
Not that she doesn't want to go to the places I want to go,

52
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:13,780
but I typically tend to be more sporadic than she is.

53
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:17,780
But if you haven't caught on to the metaphor I'm trying to draw out,

54
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:18,240
it's this,

55
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,840
that the Christian life,

56
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,800
this life of following Jesus,

57
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,060
is a pilgrimage.

58
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:24,680
It's a journey.

59
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,440
And like most pilgrimages,

60
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,740
it's far more about the journey

61
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,380
than simply arriving at the destination.

62
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:34,600
Now, don't misunderstand me.

63
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,120
The destination matters, right?

64
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,580
But it's not ours to control.

65
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,920
See, the destination for the follower of Jesus

66
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,160
is the city of God,

67
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,240
the resurrection of the body,

68
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,800
and the final joy of his presence.

69
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,560
That's in God's hands.

70
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:50,560
That's his domain, right?

71
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,520
We're comfortable with that.

72
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:55,340
What I think is in our hands, though,

73
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:55,920
is the journey.

74
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,020
The miles.

75
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:00,100
Conversations.

76
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,800
The prayers.

77
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,560
And the tears.

78
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:07,520
The moments when your feet may feel steady.

79
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,560
And also the moments

80
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,360
where you feel like the road might be endless.

81
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:15,280
Those are ours to walk together

82
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,740
as a covenant people of God.

83
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:19,960
And here's the thing about a journey.

84
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,060
God shapes us on the road.

85
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:24,760
The Christian life is not just about

86
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,720
sitting on the side of the road

87
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,440
and waiting for heaven.

88
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:30,600
Amen.

89
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,160
No.

90
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,800
No, this journey,

91
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,180
the pilgrimage,

92
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:37,860
is meant to form us

93
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:39,720
as followers of Jesus along the way.

94
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:42,080
We can either be people

95
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,500
who beeline to the destination,

96
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,500
or we can be people

97
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:47,720
who take in the beauty and sights along the way,

98
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,760
making time for rest stops

99
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:50,920
and pictures

100
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,480
and take time

101
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:54,180
and make room for the lessons

102
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:55,320
that God has for us.

103
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:58,340
I believe God has called us

104
00:05:58,340 --> 00:05:59,740
to be pilgrims

105
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:02,540
and not just tourists

106
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:04,200
in this journey.

107
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,700
And that's the heart posture

108
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,280
I want to bring to the message today.

109
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,820
And it's why I think it's good

110
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:10,820
to park our cart here

111
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:12,180
at the Psalms of Ascent.

112
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,300
See, a tourist goes sightseeing

113
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:17,680
and focuses on the sights around them.

114
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,500
We've all been there, right?

115
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,960
But a pilgrim

116
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,800
sets out to discover

117
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,200
themselves.

118
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,080
The tourist

119
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:28,500
takes a vacation

120
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,520
to get away

121
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:30,300
from the life

122
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,440
of who they normally are.

123
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:34,360
A pilgrim

124
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,500
travels to find out

125
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,740
who they really are.

126
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,220
A tourist grows

127
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,360
their collection of photographs

128
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:41,940
and souvenirs,

129
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:43,180
but a pilgrim,

130
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:43,960
I would argue,

131
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,580
grows in their love of Jesus.

132
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:48,060
A tourist

133
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:49,240
never affects

134
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:49,900
any real change

135
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:50,520
in their environment,

136
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,400
the place they visit.

137
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:53,580
But a pilgrim,

138
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,300
a pilgrim works

139
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:56,100
to see God's presence

140
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,980
in every destination

141
00:06:57,980 --> 00:06:58,660
they touch.

142
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:00,840
So this journey,

143
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:01,700
and as we walk

144
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:02,360
through the Psalms

145
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,120
of Ascent together,

146
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,100
I would ask you

147
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:05,260
to wrestle with this question.

148
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:08,180
Am I a tourist

149
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,580
or am I a pilgrim

150
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,680
in this life

151
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,920
that Jesus has called me to?

152
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:15,800
See, as we'll see today,

153
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,580
these songs

154
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:17,940
were written for travelers.

155
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:19,400
They're road songs

156
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,180
for the soul.

157
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,860
They help us to remember

158
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:22,900
that the walk itself,

159
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:23,660
the days,

160
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:24,600
the seasons,

161
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,780
and the companions

162
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,020
along the way

163
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:28,440
is where God

164
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,560
does some of his best work.

165
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:32,140
These 15 Psalms,

166
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:32,480
again,

167
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:34,140
Psalm 120 to 134,

168
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:36,080
these are the traveling songs

169
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:36,920
of God's people.

170
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,020
They were sung

171
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:38,660
by pilgrims

172
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:39,120
on their way

173
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,280
up to Jerusalem

174
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,160
for the great feast,

175
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,280
Passover,

176
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,560
Pentecost,

177
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,820
and the Feast of Tabernacles.

178
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:46,860
So while scholars

179
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:47,800
would argue over

180
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,960
what ascent really means

181
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:50,560
in the context

182
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,100
of the Psalms,

183
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,720
the most widely supported idea

184
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,160
is that these were songs

185
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:54,600
sung

186
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,560
and prayed

187
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,360
by pilgrims

188
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:56,880
on their way

189
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:57,360
to Jerusalem

190
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:57,940
for the feast.

191
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,380
No matter where

192
00:07:59,380 --> 00:07:59,960
these pilgrims

193
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,660
were coming from,

194
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:01,540
their journey

195
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,480
would have an ascent

196
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,560
towards Jerusalem

197
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,460
because it's situated

198
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:05,280
on the topographical

199
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:05,800
high point.

200
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,020
But not only

201
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,100
did it sit physically

202
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:09,700
on the high point,

203
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,560
it also represents

204
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,560
a spiritual high point,

205
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:12,780
the place where God

206
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:13,540
chose to dwell

207
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:14,220
with his people.

208
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:15,420
See,

209
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:18,220
these journeying prayers

210
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:19,220
provided a soundtrack

211
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:19,940
for God's people.

212
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:22,360
confession time.

213
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,280
This is for me,

214
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:23,860
not for you all.

215
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:24,900
You guys are good church people.

216
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:25,760
But those,

217
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:26,800
these playlists

218
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:27,820
are probably more

219
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:28,560
God-honoring

220
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,220
than our typical playlists.

221
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:31,960
But I digress.

222
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:34,820
These 15 Psalms

223
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,560
were a soundtrack,

224
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:36,600
a worship set

225
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,660
for the people of God,

226
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:39,800
a people on journey.

227
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,060
These Psalms reminded

228
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:42,500
the people

229
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:43,500
of their nomadic roots

230
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:44,020
in Abraham

231
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,600
and the liberation journey

232
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,080
of the Exodus

233
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:46,660
with Moses.

234
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:49,380
These pilgrimages

235
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:50,900
served as a reminder

236
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:51,600
to God's people

237
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,140
that they were

238
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:53,440
a pilgrim people

239
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,120
on journey with God.

240
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,340
Invite us to think

241
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:58,060
about these Psalms

242
00:08:58,060 --> 00:08:59,000
as we go through this

243
00:08:59,000 --> 00:08:59,780
the same way.

244
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:00,960
They remind us

245
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,820
that our life

246
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:03,600
with God

247
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,280
is a journey.

248
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,300
It's a journey with God,

249
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:07,140
but it's also a journey

250
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:08,580
with his people

251
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:10,560
on our way

252
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:11,660
to God's eternal kingdom.

253
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:13,820
The writer of Hebrews

254
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:14,920
describes God's people

255
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:15,560
as foreigners

256
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,540
and strangers

257
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:17,780
looking for a country

258
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:18,300
of their own.

259
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:19,760
I invite us

260
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:20,400
to think about it

261
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:20,980
the same way

262
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:23,240
and join in the Psalms

263
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:23,640
of Ascent

264
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:24,620
and sing praise

265
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,180
and pray a soundtrack

266
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,500
for the pilgrimage

267
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,180
of our life

268
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:28,620
with God

269
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:30,740
not to physical Jerusalem

270
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,960
but to the eternal country

271
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:32,780
of new heaven and earth

272
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,080
that lie before us

273
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:34,520
with God.

274
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:36,940
I think if you're in it

275
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:37,600
and I just finished

276
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,660
a spiritual formation class

277
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,160
so I'm all about

278
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,320
imagining stuff.

279
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,760
I think you can picture

280
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,580
whole families

281
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:43,740
and villages

282
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:45,320
setting out together

283
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:45,780
sandals

284
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:46,940
hitting the dirt

285
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:48,840
children

286
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,420
running ahead

